    {
      "name": "part-panel",
      "aria": "The approach",
      "segment": "part",
      "z": 10,
      "top": "61%",
      "html": "      <h2>The canyon does the reveal for you.</h2>\n      <p>Nothing of Al-Khazneh is visible until the Siq allows it. The walls hold the view back for a kilometre, then release it all at once.</p>\n      <dl class=\"facts\"><div><dt>1.2km</dt><dd>Length of the Siq approach</dd></div><div><dt>40m</dt><dd>Height of the carved facade</dd></div></dl>"
    },
    {
      "name": "close-panel",
      "aria": "The carving",
      "segment": "close",
      "z": 10,
      "top": "28%",
      "html": "      <h2>Cut down, not built up.</h2>\n      <p>Carved from the cornice downward, straight into the cliff, so nothing could be corrected once the chisel had passed.</p>"
    },
    {
      "name": "open-panel",
      "aria": "Beyond the city",
      "segment": "open",
      "z": 10,
      "top": "42%",
      "html": "      <h2>And then the desert takes over.</h2>\n      <p>Past the tombs the sandstone opens into Wadi Rum, where the same rock that was carved into a treasury is simply left standing.</p>\n      <button class=\"note-button\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span><span>Plan the route</span></button>"
    }
